# Build context for the root image (`docker build .`).
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST, not a denylist. A developer's checkout carries untracked
# material that must never reach an image layer: a filled-in .mcp.json,
# config/models.json with API keys, bots/, nested bundle .git directories, Python
# .venv trees, SQLite databases and *.bak copies. A denylist has to name every one
# of those (and misses the next one added); an allowlist ships only what is named.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: the LAST matching line wins, so the four blocks below must stay
# in this order.

# ─── 1. Everything is out unless a later line says otherwise ────────────────
*

# ─── 2. …re-included: exactly what the image runs on ────────────────────────
# `scripts/init-db.js` walks scripts/ (migrations included) and the gateway
# imports bundles/ and registry/ at runtime, so the source tree beyond servers/
# has to be here. The env and model templates are read by scripts/setup.js and
# by bundle installs to seed a real, untracked .env.
!servers
!scripts
!bundles
!registry
!skills
!templates
!vendor
!package.json
!package-lock.json
# The MIT notice has to ship with the image, and LICENSE is a plain file the
# blanket `*` above would otherwise keep out.
!LICENSE
!.env.example
!.env.garage.example
!models.example.json
!.mcp.json.example
!docker-compose.yml

# ─── 3. …but never these, at any depth ──────────────────────────────────────
# VCS data (a nested bundle .git carries a whole history), dependencies, Python
# caches and venvs, secrets and keys, runtime databases and logs, and the
# per-machine files that hold tokens. Note that `servers/gateway/secrets/` is
# TRACKED CODE and is deliberately absent from this list — there is no `secrets`
# pattern here.
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/.ruff_cache
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.gpg
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/.npmrc
**/.netrc
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite-*
**/*.bak
**/*.bak-*
**/*.log
**/.crow
**/.mcp.json
**/models.json

# ─── 4. …with the shipped env TEMPLATES still re-included ───────────────────
# Block 3's `**/.env.*` swallows `.env.example`, so every template is re-included
# again HERE, below every exclusion (the last matching line wins).
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
!.env.garage.example